+/*
+ * (0355) The charger alone, two reads, for the fast poll that owns the plug
+ * icon.  The MAX77854 keeps the cable's state in its *status* bytes, B2 bit 6
+ * CHGIN_OK and B3 bits 6:5 CHGIN_DTLS, which follow the input live: only their
+ * copies in the latched interrupt register B0 (CHGIN_I, bits 6 and 5:4) hold
+ * the last edge until it is read, so the status alone never sticks at 1 after
+ * an unplug.  Reading B0 here would be wrong in the other direction: clearing
+ * it every 500 ms would discard the edge the charger driver wants.
+ *
+ * Returns 0 when both reads answered, -1 otherwise; either way the published
+ * state is the one just read, and a failed read means "no cable".
+ */
+/*
+ * (0365) The gauge's Current register (0x0A) as a signed value.  The gauge is
+ * the one block on this chip that has always answered, and its current is a
+ * direct physical statement: positive means charge into the battery.
